/	PDP-12 TANK GAME

/	THIS IS A TANK GAME FOR THE PDP-12.  AT THIS POINT THE ORIGINAL AUTHOR
/	IS UNKNOWN.  IT IS UNCLEAR IF ANY IMPORTANT RESOURCES OF OS/8 ARE USED
/	AND THE SAVE IMAGE INDICATES IT LOADS INTO LESS THAN 4K OF MEMORY.

/	HOWEVER, IT *DOES* (AT LEAST MODESTLY) INTERACT WITH OS/8; TIME WILL
/	TELL IF THIS IS MORE THAN SUPERFICIAL.  IF POSSIBLE, COMPATIBILITY WITH
/	DIAL AND/OR P?S/8 WOULD BE USEFUL.

/	INITIAL DISASSEMBLY AND CLEANUP: CHARLES LASNER

/	IF THE MOOD STRIKES, MORE WORK CAN BE DONE TO FIGURE OUT WHAT IS GOING
/	ON IN A MORE COHERENT MANNER.

/	LAST EDIT: 30-NOV-2018	CJL

/	NOTE: THIS PROGRAM IS PARTIALLY WRITEN IN LINC MODE CODE; AS SUCH, IT
/	REQUIRES A DUAL-MODE ASSEMBLER SUCH AS P?S/8 PAL WITH THE /8 COMMMAND-
/	LINE OPTION SWITCH SET.  IT IS LIKELY ONE OF THE USER-WRITTEN PAL12
/	ASSEMBLERS CAN ALSO HANDLE THE REQUIREMENT, BUT THIS HAS NOT BEEN
/	RESEARCHED; WHEN IN DOUBT, COMPARE TO THE OUTPUT OF P?S/8 PAL.

/	CHECK IF STARTED IN WRONG MODE [OR LINC MODE ASSEMBLY IS UNAVAILABLE].

/	IFNZRO	7402-HLT	<

	PMODE				/ENSURE STARTED IN PDP-8 MODE FOR NOW.

				>

	LMODE				/GOTO LINC MODE [IF POSSIBLE].

	IFNZRO	HLT		<

	ERROR	.			/THIS IS NOT A DUAL-MODE ASSEMBLER!

				>

	PMODE				/START IN PDP-8 MODE.				
/	EQUATED SYMBOLS.

/	DISASSEMBLER-REQUIRED SYMBOLS.  STUDY THE CODE TO ELIMINATE THEM IF POSSIBLE.

	V50=	5450
	W00=	5600
	W174=	5774
	W176=	5776
	XA47=	6247
	XE71=	7271
	XE174=	7374
	XF114=	7514

/	STANDARD FAMILY-OF-8 MICRO-OPERATE COMBINED OPERATIONS.

	NL0000=	CLA			/SET AC TO 0000.
	NL0001=	CLA IAC			/SET AC TO 0001.
	NL0002=	CLA CLL CML RTL		/SET AC TO 0002.
	NL2000=	CLA CLL CML RTR		/SET AC TO 2000.
	NL3777=	CLA CLL CMA RAR		/SET AC TO 3777.
	NL4000=	CLA CLL CML RAR		/SET AC TO 4000.
	NL5777=	CLA CLL CMA RTR		/SET AC TO 5777.
	NL7775=	CLA CLL CMA RTL		/SET AC TO 7775.
	NL7776=	CLA CLL CMA RAL		/SET AC TO 7776.
	NL7777=	CLA CMA			/SET AC TO 7777.
/	NOTES TO FUTURE MAINTAINERS FROM CHARLES LASNER:

/	1) THIS IS A DISASSEMBLY OF A PARTICULARLY "DIRTY" CORE IMAGE OF THE
/	   PROGRAM, WHICH IS LARGELY A "DISEASE" BORNE OF TYPICAL SLOPPY
/	   PRACTICE ENCOURAGED BY THE MEAGER FACILITIES OF OS/8.

/	   IF YOU INSIST ON USING OS/8, AT LEAST ADD APPROPRIATE ZBLOCK STATEMENTS
/	   TO PRE-CLEAR MEMORY SO THE CORE-IMAGE HAS NO JUNK IN IT.  NEEDLESS TO
/	   SAY, THIS WAS NOT DONE, THUS THE PREDICTABLE MESS OF NOT BEING ALL
/	   THAT SURE THAT WHAT YOU ARE LOOKING AT IS EVEN PART OF THE INTENTION
/	   OF THE ORIGINAL AUTHOR.

/	   NOTE: P?S/8 NEVER HAS THIS PROBLEM AS THERE ARE OPTION SWITCHES IN THE
/	   P?S/8 BINARY LOADER TO PRESET ALL MEMORY TO YOUR CHOICE OF 7402 (THE
/	   PDP-8 HLT INSTRUCTION) OR 0000 (WHICH IS PREFERABLE AND ALSO IS THE
/	   LINC HLT INSTRUCTION).  AS A RESULT, ALL PROGRAMS *PROPERLY* CREATED
/	   ARE FAR EASIER TO RECONSTRUCT.  uNFORTUNATELY, IF THIS IS ALL YOU HAVE
/	   TO WORK WITH, THE WARNINGS ONLY HELP YOU IN YOUR NEXT PROJECT, NOT HERE.

/	2) I AM NOT CONVINCED THIS IS INHERENTLY A PDP-12 PROGRAM.  MANY SUCH
/	   GAMES-TYPE PROGRAMS ARE ADAPTATIONS FROM OTHER PDP-8 FAMILY PROGRAMS
/	   WHERE THE CODE IS JUST SLIGHTLY ALTERED FOR PDP-12 USAGE.  IF ANOTHER
/	   SOURCE FILE (OR EVEN A BINARY FILE!) CAN BE LOCATED, IT CAN HELP TO
/	   ELIMINATE MUCH OF THE DISTRACTING JUNK, ETC.

/	3) I AM ALSO NOT CONVINCED THIS IS AN INHERENTLY OS/8-SPECIFIC PROGRAM
/	   BECAUSE SOME OF THE OS/8-ISMS ARE NAIVE.  THIS WOULD BE THE CASE WHEN
/	   AN AMATEUR DOES A QUICK-AND-DIRTY MOVE TO OS/8 WITH THE TYPICAL LEVEL
/	   OF IGNORANCE (WHICH IS PART AND PARCEL OF THE REST OF THE PROBLEMS).

/	4) BECAUSE THIS IS AN IGNORANT DISASSEMBLY AND NOT MUCH HUMAN CODE EFFORT
/	   APPLIED YET, THERE ARE STILL ARTIFACTS OF THE SIMPLISTIC PROCESSS.  WORSE
/	   STILL, SINCE THE PROGRAM DOES USE EAE, THE USE OF EAE SYMBOLS WAS
/	   ENABLED; UNFORTUNATELY, THAT MEANS YOU ALSO GET PDP-8/E MODE "B"
/	   INSTRUCTION SUPPORT, WHICH CLEARLY IS IRRELEVANT TO A PROGRAM KNOWN TO
/	   RUN ON A PDP-12.  AS SUCH, THERE IS ANOTHER LAYER TO CLEANING THIS UP IF
/	   PURSUING IT IS NECESSARY (WHICH IS LIKELY).  ANY USE OF PDP-8/E EAE
/	   EXTENSIONS HAS TO BE ELIMINATED AS ONE OF BUT MANY SANITY CHECKS THAT
/	   STILL HAVE TO BE APPLIED TO THE CODE AS I LAST WORKED ON IT.

/	   NOTE: IT WAS EVEN WORSE WHILE I WAS WORKING ON IT BUT I AM THE FIRST TO
/	   ADMIT IT NEEDS EVEN MORE WORK TO BE HALF-WAY REASONABLE.

/	5) I RECOMMEND SOME WORK BE DONE ON PROVING CERTAIN SECTIONS ARE TRUE JUNK.
/	   THE BEST WAY TO ACCOMPLISH THAT IS TO LOAD OVER THE BINARY OF THIS
/	   SOURCE CODE (USUALLY TANK.BN) WITH SOME VERY SELECTIVE ZBLOCK SECTIONS
/	   AND TRY THE OVERLAID VERSION.  THE MORE YOU CAN ELIMINATE THE BETTER.
/	   THIS WILL ALSO ALLOW PATCHING THE CODE MORE EASILY, ETC.
